---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Cross-Industry JTBD Survey & Card Sort" description="Project detail">
  <main class="page-shell project-detail-shell">
    <article class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-header">
        <a href="/projects" class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> All case studies</a>
        <h1>Cross-Industry JTBD Survey & Card Sort</h1>
        <p class="project-intro">Ran a multi-industry research study to surface patterns in customer jobs, pains, and priorities across different operational contexts.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Client:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Product strategy team</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Role:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Research lead</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Focus:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">JTBD interviews, survey design, affinity clustering</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Preview:</span>
          <a href="#" class="meta-link">View project →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Uncovering shared and different customer needs across industries</h2>
          <p>To inform positioning and prioritization, the product team needed to understand how customer jobs, pains, and priorities varied across different industries. We designed and executed a multi-industry research study using job interviews, surveys, and card sorting.</p>
          <p>The research revealed both surprising commonalities and important differences across markets, which enabled sharper prioritization and a more nuanced go-to-market strategy.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
